IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wk-nouns`
IMPORT `wk-agreements`
IMPORT `wk-information`
IMPORT `wk-restrictive-terms`
IMPORT `wk-contractors-and-claims`
IMPORT `wk-test-fixtures`

-- POSITIVE CONTROLS. Every assertion in this file is WRONG on purpose, and must FAIL.
-- check.sh expects exactly this many failures here (and none anywhere else), so a build
-- that stopped evaluating assertions, or a rule that stopped drawing one of these
-- distinctions, turns the check red. Each states a misreading the encoding must not make.

§ `Positive controls: each assertion must fail`

-- WRONG: "the Agencies will focus on whether the businesses compete in the same labor
-- markets even if they do not compete as sellers": Acme and Bolt, selling different
-- things and hiring the same engineers, do compete for workers.
#ASSERT `General principles: whether the businesses compete for workers` `competitors for workers` EQUALS JUST `the businesses do not compete for workers in any labor market named`

-- WRONG: "Businesses that compete with each other for workers may be committing an
-- antitrust crime" is not said of potentially competing employers.
#ASSERT `1: what section 1 says of the agreement` (`an identified agreement` `potentially competing employers` `no-hire`) EQUALS JUST (LIST `businesses that compete with each other for workers may be committing an antitrust crime if they enter into such an agreement`, `even if criminal charges are not pursued, such an agreement may also be subject to civil liability`, `the agencies state that such an agreement, formed between competing or potentially competing employers, directly or through an intermediary, is illegal even if it did not result in actual harm such as lower wages`, `the DOJ may criminally investigate and, where appropriate, bring felony charges against the participants in such an agreement, including both individuals and companies`)

-- WRONG: a restraint subordinate and collateral to a joint venture and reasonably necessary
-- to it is not one the text says is illegal regardless of its effects (n.15).
#ASSERT `General principles: what the text says of whether the agreement's effects matter` (`an identified agreement with the n.15 findings` `competitors for workers` `no-hire` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST (LIST `section 1: the agencies state that such an agreement is illegal even if it did not result in actual harm such as lower wages`)

-- WRONG: a contrary finding on the exchange's effect does not leave the effect sentence
-- standing.
#ASSERT `3: what section 3 says of the exchange` (`a sensitive exchange` `competitors for workers` `directly between the businesses` `the exchange neither has nor is likely to have an anticompetitive effect`) EQUALS JUST (LIST `sharing competitively sensitive information with competitors about terms and conditions of employment may violate the antitrust laws`, `exchanging competitively sensitive compensation or other employment information with a competitor may be unlawful when the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect, whether or not that effect was intended: such an effect is found`, `information exchanges may indicate the existence of a wage-fixing conspiracy`)

-- WRONG: "such as if they function to prevent" is an example, not a condition: a training
-- repayment provision with no such finding still "can be anticompetitive" depending on the
-- facts and circumstances.
#ASSERT `5: what section 5 says of the term` (`a bare term` `a training repayment agreement provision`) EQUALS LIST `such provisions raise many of the same antitrust concerns as non-competes`, `state law also sets limits on training repayment requirements and NDA restrictions`

-- WRONG: the Overview's "false claims ... may violate federal laws against unfair,
-- deceptive, or abusive practices" is said of false claims, not of misleading ones.
#ASSERT `7: what section 7 says of the claim` (`an earnings claim` FALSE TRUE `employees`) EQUALS LIST `the Overview: false claims about workers' potential earnings may violate federal laws against unfair, deceptive, or abusive practices`, `the agencies may investigate and take action against businesses that make false or misleading claims about potential earnings that workers, including both employees and independent contractors, may realize`

-- WRONG: an exchange whose effect has not been assessed does not get the effect sentence in
-- a pending form; the answer turns on the effect (fork F12).
#ASSERT `3: what section 3 says of the exchange` (`a sensitive exchange` `competitors for workers` `directly between the businesses` `the exchange's effect has not been assessed`) EQUALS JUST (LIST `sharing competitively sensitive information with competitors about terms and conditions of employment may violate the antitrust laws`, `exchanging competitively sensitive compensation or other employment information with a competitor may be unlawful when the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect, whether or not that effect was intended: its effect has not been assessed`, `information exchanges may indicate the existence of a wage-fixing conspiracy`)

-- WRONG: a finding on potential competition that has not been made is not the contrary
-- finding (fork F1).
#ASSERT `General principles: whether the businesses compete for workers` `businesses with no finding on potential competition` EQUALS JUST `the businesses do not compete for workers in any labor market named`

-- WRONG: section 2's per se sentence is read as said of a franchisor and franchisee that
-- compete for workers (fork F7); one that does not compete gets the scrutiny sentence only.
#ASSERT `2: what section 2 says of the agreement` (`an identified franchise agreement` `businesses that do not compete for workers` `no-hire` `a franchisor and its franchisee` FALSE) EQUALS JUST (LIST `no-poach clauses in franchise agreements are subject to antitrust scrutiny`, `the agencies state that such an agreement between a franchisor and its franchisee not to compete for workers can be per se illegal under the antitrust laws: the agreement itself may be illegal regardless of whether it actually harms workers`)
